# Sends SIGSTOP or SIGCONT to the running "python3 inference_server.py"
# process — a thin service wrapper around
# CalibrationOrchestratorNode::signalInferenceServer(), which already does
# exactly this (scans /proc for the process, signals it) for the entire
# duration of a ~/calibrate run. Exposed as a service so
# calibration_broadcaster_node (package aruco_perception, not orchestrator
# — cannot call the orchestrator's private member function directly across
# that package boundary) can reuse the same signalling implementation at a
# per-waypoint grain for hybrid_per_waypoint_enabled mode, instead of a
# second, divergent /proc-scan-and-signal implementation.
#
# stop: true = SIGSTOP (pause, ~0% CPU while stopped), false = SIGCONT
# (resume).
bool stop
---
bool success
string message
